.TH CANDOR 1 "Saphira Candor" "Saphira Candor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
candor \- answer questions from witnessed facts first, neural guesses marked
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B candor ask --model
.I F
.B --witness
.I F
.B --context
.I T
.RB [ --question
.IR T ]
.B --candidate
.I A
.RB [ --candidate
.IR B ...]
.RB [ --head
.IR forward | inverse | both ]
.RB [ --json ]
.br
.B candor train --data
.I F
.B --val
.I F
.B --out
.I F
.RB [ --epochs
.IR n ]
.RB [ --seed
.IR n ]
.RB [ --n-opt
.IR n ]
.RB [ --init-model
.IR F ]
.RB [ --q2 | --q3 | --q4 | --q8 ]
.br
.B candor --help | --version
.br
.B candor --about
.RB [ --model
.IR F ]
.RB [ --witness
.IR F ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcandor\fR is the full Candor engine: an external model plus external
witnessed memory, with training included. It answers from exact witnessed
facts first and says so; anything else runs the neural forward pass, marked
as a guess. Retraining is an ordinary command, not a separate product.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ask
Answer one question. Requires \fB--model\fR, \fB--context\fR, and at least one
\fB--candidate\fR. \fB--witness\fR enables the fact-first path; without it
every answer comes from the forward pass.
.TP
.B train
Teach witnessed facts: \fB--data\fR rows (context/options/label, plus
\fBentity\fR+\fBfact\fR keys to register memories), validated against
\fB--val\fR, written to \fB--out\fR. The best-validation checkpoint is kept
automatically. \fB--init-model\fR continues from an existing checkpoint
instead of from scratch. \fB--q2|--q3|--q4|--q8\fR store smaller
quantized checkpoints (storage only; compute stays float32).
See TRAINING.md for the full discipline: how, why, when, and when not to.
.SH VERDICTS
Every answer carries exactly one verdict:
.TP
.B REMEMBERED
Exactly one candidate matches a witnessed (entity, property) fact. The source
statement is printed and the neural forward pass is skipped entirely.
.TP
.B GUESSED
No exact fact answered. The forward pass runs and its scores/probabilities are
reported, marked as a guess. A guess is never presented as a memory.
.PP
Absence is never a denial: an unwitnessed candidate is reported as not in
memory, never as false.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --model " F"
Model checkpoint file (SNE1 container, v1-v5).
.TP
.BR --witness " F"
Witnessed-fact JSONL (rows carrying \fBentity\fR + \fBfact\fR keys).
.TP
.BR --context " T" ", " --question " T"
Question text. The entity is resolved from the context against known witnesses.
.TP
.BR --candidate " A"
One answer option; repeatable, up to 64.
.TP
.BR --head " forward|inverse|both"
Which judgement head answers (default forward).
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable output: \fB{"verdict": "remembered"|"guessed", ...}\fR.
.TP
.BR --version ", " --about
\fB--version\fR prints the engine version. \fB--about\fR prints engine
provenance, plus sha256 of any \fB--model\fR/\fB--witness\fR files supplied.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Answered (either verdict).
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure (unreadable model, corrupt container, no forward possible).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
candor ask --model models/model.q8 --witness witnesses/witness.jsonl \\
  --context "What is true of the tract0007 pipit?" \\
  --candidate alert --candidate louder
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scandor (1)
